This repository builds on the Portable Video Research Group's (PVRG)
MPEG-1 codec, developed at Stanford University. PVRG placed this codec in
the public domain, subject to one condition stated in their original
distribution:

    "References related to these codecs should NOT use any author's name,
    or refer to Stanford University. Rather the Portable Video Research
    Group or the acronym (PVRG) should be used, such as PVRG-MPEG,
    PVRG-P64, PVRG-JPEG."

This repository honours that condition: references here use "PVRG" or
"PVRG-MPEG", not individual author names or "Stanford University", when
referring to the codec's origin. This condition does not restrict copying,
modification, or redistribution — only how the codec's origin may be
described.

Source vendored into source/ is taken from:
    https://github.com/maikmerten/mpeg
    (a patched-to-build mirror of PVRG-MPEG v1.2.x, itself sourced from the
    original public-domain release; the exact commit is recorded in
    source/PROVENANCE.md)

The files in original-1993-release/ are Graham Logan's own 1993 DOS port
of PVRG-MPEG, republished here by the original author.
